@title Postmortem: INC-2291 Billing API outage
@subtitle Billing Platform · Brightwave Telecom · 2026-09-03

kpi Duration | 47 min
kpi Peak error rate | 38.5%
kpi Failed requests | 182,400
kpi Customers affected | 12,900

# Summary

A config change lowered the database connection pool from 200 to 20. Requests queued and timed out. The change was rolled back.

# Timeline

table = Time (UTC),Event; 14:02,config change merged and deployed; 14:06,error rate alert fires; 14:09,on-call acknowledges; 14:21,incident declared Sev2; 14:33,connection pool exhaustion identified; 14:41,rollback started; 14:49,errors return to baseline; 14:53,incident resolved

# Error rate

data errs = time,Error rate; 14:00,0.2; 14:05,4.1; 14:10,17.8; 14:15,29.6; 14:20,38.5; 14:25,36.9; 14:30,37.2; 14:35,35.0; 14:40,33.4; 14:45,12.7; 14:50,0.6; 14:55,0.3
chart line errs x=time y=Error rate unit=% title="Error rate, 5 minute intervals"

# Root cause

The pool size was set to 20 instead of 200, far too small for peak request volume. Requests waited for a free connection and timed out, which drove the error rate up.

! The config linter did not validate pool size bounds, so the bad value passed review and reached production.

# Action items

table = Action,Owner,Due; add bounds validation for pool settings,Marta Kowalski,2026-09-24; canary config changes to 5% of pods first,Ravi Shah,2026-10-08; alert on pool saturation above 80%,Billing on-call,2026-09-17
